<title>JAPAN: Sumitomo Metal gold mine output highest in Japan.</title>
<headline>Sumitomo Metal gold mine output highest in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sumitomo Metal Mining Co Ltd said on Tuesday that output at its Hishikari gold mine in Kagoshima prefecture, southern Japan, has totalled 83.1 tonnes since it started production in 1985, making it Japan's biggest ever gold producer.</p>
<p>It took Mitsubishi Materials Corp's Sado mine in Niigata prefecture, northern Japan, 380 years to produce 83 tonnes of gold. The Sado mine was closed in 1989.</p>
<p>The Hishikari mine currently produces about seven or eight tonnes of gold annually, accounting for more than 90 percent of domestic gold production.</p>
<p>The potential gold reserves still in the mine are estimated to be at about 180 tonnes, it said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
